  clock: 2  # d10d
  nonce: d10d  # d10d
  message: "RULING 2026-09-25, delegated by the owner (\"investigate and rule in the hypergumbo spirit\"). Measured on dev 7821064366. Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/vogos_09252026/ (fixtures fx/, outputs out/ + corpus/, arm driver run_arm.sh). Arm B = ~/hg_arms/vogos_B, a detached worktree with ONLY javascript.yaml changed: http/https/net.createServer, dgram.createSocket and Deno.listen/listenTls/listenDatagram moved net_recv -> net_listen. Separate XDG_CACHE_HOME per arm.\n\n**RULING: DO NOT RETAG YET. THE HOLD STAYS, FOR TWO NEW REASONS THAT ARE TRUE TODAY. The destination is settled; the licence is not.** This is not wont_do. Ruling 1 already classifies every one of these rows as a deferred crossing: createServer and createSocket return a server/socket handle, and the Deno calls return a listener or conn handle; the bytes arrive at a callback or a later read. So the rows are misdeclared, and they move once the two conditions below hold.\n\nREASON 1 -- A RETAG TODAY SHIPS A FALSE ALL-CLEAR (ruling 2 clause 3 / ruling 3). Filed as INV-fogum, which now blocks this item. The net_listen shadow reaches only the BOUNDARY arm: `deferred_crossing_sites` is read in `_verify_claim_uncredited` (verify_claims.py:4514) and never in `_verify_taint_claim_uncredited` (:5084).\n\nFixture fx/node_http_clean:\n\n    function handle(req, res) { fs.writeFileSync('/var/data/' + req.url, 'x'); }\n    http.createServer(handle);\n\n    arm A (dev)   untrusted-input-no-host-fs  violated\n    arm B         untrusted-input-no-host-fs  confirmed   (bare, no caveat, rc 0 on that claim)\n                  no-net-recv (boundary claim) confirmed_with_caveats [deferred_crossing: http.createServer]\n\nIn one invocation, the boundary verdict discloses the listen site and the taint verdict certifies the server clean. The same asymmetry is ALREADY LIVE on dev in Go (fx/go_clean2: `ServeHTTP` writes \"/var/data/\"+r.URL.Path; untrusted-input-no-host-fs is a bare `confirmed`). There it was not created by the Go retag: an arm with ListenAndServe put back under net_recv, ~/hg_arms/vogos_G, is also bare `confirmed`, because Go's handler is not call-reachable from main. It is created in JavaScript, where it would turn a violated verdict into a clean one.\n\nREASON 2 -- IN JAVASCRIPT THE LAUNCH MINT IS LOAD-BEARING FOR TRUE VERDICTS, AND NO CATALOGUE ROW CAN REPLACE IT. This is 0010's \"shape does not predict worth\", in a new form.\n- createServer takes its ARRIVAL SCOPE AS AN ARGUMENT, and the analyzer links it. The fx/node_http finding's path is `server.js file -> handle -> _cb_on@16 -> fs.writeFileSync(..., body)`, where body is accumulated from req 'data' chunks. The verdict is TRUE: the program writes network input to disk. By measurement 0001's letter the finding is FP-attributed, because body does not derive from createServer's return value. But the violated VERDICT is correct.\n- In arm B the same program is `confirmed_with_caveats` with ONLY an unrelated `unknown_receiver_scope` caveat (end/listen/on). Once INV-fogum ships, that becomes a caveated confirm, which is ADR-0049 §Consequences' \"real loss\". The ADR accepts that loss only \"where no arrival scope resolves\". Here it DOES resolve: it is the callback argument of the launch call.\n- The four moved languages met ruling 3 by KEEPING a transfer row: net.Listener.Accept / net.Conn.Read, socket.recv, Network.Socket.recv, gen_tcp.recv (TestServerLaunchIsADeferredCrossing::test_the_real_receive_is_still_rowed_in_every_moved_language). JavaScript has no server-side transfer to keep. Node's request and socket bytes are callback-delivered (req.on('data'), socket.on('data'), dgram 'message'), and no row exists for IncomingMessage or net.Socket receive. The server fixtures confirm it: node_http, node_net and deno each have net_recv 1 -> 0 chains in arm B.\n- The surviving surface WI-dosuh made reachable (WebSocket / EventSource addEventListener/onmessage) is the browser CLIENT side. fx/ws_client keeps its net_recv chain in both arms, but it represents no server's ingress.\n- The one exception is Deno's Listener.accept() / Conn.read(), which ARE transfers and could be rowed. In fx/deno, `conn` comes from `for await (const conn of listener)` and is untyped. I did NOT verify whether such rows would fire.\n\nCORPUS (0010's bar, per repo as this item's counterweight asks). Nine repositories whose production code calls a launch row: express, pm2, apollo-server, y-webrtc, networked-aframe, polis, gemini-cli, nest, vite.\n\n    net_recv chains A -> B:  express 1->0  pm2 29->0  apollo-server 1->0  y-webrtc 1->0\n                             networked-aframe 2->0  polis 1->0  nest 4->0\n                             gemini-cli 5->1  vite 3->1        total 47 -> 2\n    (the two survivors are EventSource/WebSocket.addEventListener: client receives)\n    untrusted-input-* verdicts: 27 per arm, 0 changed.\n    launch-rooted violating flows in arm A: 0. Every violated flow is ipc_recv-origin (pm2, gemini-cli, vite); everything else is `inconclusive` on the coverage gate.\n\nSo the corpus supplies NO adjudicable launch-rooted finding. That is the Phoenix.Router position (\"absence of findings is not evidence of harmlessness\"). The measured effect on shipped verdicts in this cohort would be ZERO, and it must be recorded as zero, not as a precision gain. Seven of nine repos lose every net_recv chain: the per-repo ruling-3 counterweight bites in 7/9.\n\nLICENCE -- the retag moves when BOTH hold:\n (a) INV-fogum is satisfied: a clean taint verdict whose source label derives from a shadowed boundary carries the deferred_crossing caveat. Control: go_clean2 on dev goes from bare `confirmed` to `confirmed_with_caveats[deferred_crossing]`.\n (b) The arrival scope is represented, via WI-ritog's tier 1 or a JS-first slice of it: the FUNCTION ARGUMENT of a net_listen call (createServer/net.createServer's request/connection listener, dgram's 'message' listener) is seeded start_at:callee as untrusted_input. Proof, run not reasoned:\n     - fx/node_http stays `violated` in the retag arm.\n     - fx/node_http_pure (a literal write in writeLog() BEFORE the launch: the 0010 LAUNCH-FP shape) goes to `confirmed_with_caveats[deferred_crossing]`, not `violated`.\n     - fx/node_http_clean is never a bare `confirmed`.\n     - The nine-repo corpus is re-run with no verdict moving to a bare `confirmed`.\n I did not add an isbefore from WI-ritog. The owner or main session should add `WI-ritog --add-isbefore WI-vogos` if (b) is accepted as stated.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION PLAN (once (a) and (b) hold; one PR, catalogue + tests + docs):\n 1. javascript.yaml: move http/https/net.createServer, dgram.createSocket and Deno.listen/listenTls/listenDatagram into a `net_listen:` section, with the go.yaml-style SETUP/LAUNCH notes. Also correct the STALE REACH notes on the EventSource and WebSocket rows: they still say onmessage/onclose are \"declared unreachable in analyzer_disclosure.CONSTRUCT_BLIND_ROWS\", which WI-dosuh removed.\n 2. tests/test_inv_nular_false_sources.py:\n    - Delete F2_EXEMPT[\"javascript\"]; test_f2_exemptions_still_have_something_to_exempt forces that, since Deno.listen matches the predicate.\n    - Convert test_javascript_did_not_move_and_the_reason_was_measured into rows of test_the_launch_family_is_disclosed_not_minted.\n    - Add a JS represented-crossing test that asserts on the ARRIVAL SEED rather than a transfer row, because there is none to assert. Keep the Phoenix test separate.\n 3. ADR-0049 §Implementation state: replace \"JavaScript is F2_EXEMPT ...\" with the moved state. Name the licence (arrival seeding, not a kept transfer row) as a THIRD form of the ruling-3 proof, beside \"transfer row kept\" (the four) and \"never fired\" (swift NWListener). Correct the gocryptfs attribution (INV-fogum's description). Update docs/hypergumbo-spec.md's ADR-0049 auto-derivation section to match.\n 4. Measured effect to publish: the corpus A/B above, re-run, plus the fixture table.\n\nNOT VERIFIED: whether Deno.Listener.accept / Deno.Conn.read rows would fire; gocryptfs re-run (not on disk); any repo outside the nine; whether a JS request handler registered through express/koa (not createServer's argument) is reachable from the launch. express's app.listen passes `this`, not a function."  # d10d
